{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788122190151,"sessionID":"ses_fab9cc058ffexEheteSaWDsSOK","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_01a054634f1670b39f4351675b413ba7","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/Ori/Documents/Projects/BunkerGame/docs/director/GAME-VISION.md"},"output":"<path>/Users/Ori/Documents/Projects/BunkerGame/docs/director/GAME-VISION.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # THE OUTSKIRTS — Game Vision\n2: \n3: ## Identity\n4: \n5: **Game:** THE OUTSKIRTS\n6: \n7: THE OUTSKIRTS is an atmospheric survival game. The target is a polished,\n8: cohesive experience rather than a basic Roblox blockout or a collection of\n9: unconnected systems.\n10: \n11: ## Target Experience\n12: \n13: The player should feel vulnerable, curious, and motivated to make an abandoned\n14: place functional again. Environments, gameplay systems, lighting, sound, UI,\n15: and progression should ultimately support the same survival atmosphere.\n16: \n17: The intended quality bar is:\n18: \n19: - atmospheric\n20: - detailed\n21: - intentionally composed\n22: - abandoned but functional\n23: - survival-oriented\n24: - visually cohesive\n25: - significantly more polished than the current bunker\n26: \n27: ## Starting Experience\n28: \n29: The player wakes near an old bed inside a creepy, abandoned underground bunker\n30: bedroom.\n31: \n32: The bedroom is the first readable space in a larger bunker. It must establish:\n33: \n34: - where the player has awakened\n35: - that the bunker is old, neglected, and still partly functional\n36: - a clear visual route toward the rest of the bunker\n37: - the survival tone of the wider game\n38: \n39: The bedroom must connect into a larger bunker. It is not an isolated box and\n40: must not be treated as a standalone final environment.\n41: \n42: ## Bunker Vision\n43: \n44: The bunker should be a sequence of purposeful, connected spaces rather than one\n45: rectangular room. The layout should eventually support:\n46: \n47: - bedroom/start area\n48: - central bunker/common area\n49: - weapon/workbench area\n50: - upgrade area\n51: - storage\n52: - power/electrical infrastructure\n53: - NPC/shop area\n54: - access toward farming and the outside\n55: - bunker entrance/defense point\n56: \n57: These are spatial and long-term functional requirements. Missing gameplay\n58: behavior must not be invented during environment planning.\n59: \n60: ## Broader Gameplay Vision\n61: \n62: Long-term concepts include:\n63: \n64: - realistic-feeling rifle and combat gameplay\n65: - pickaxe/tool gameplay\n66: - torch/flashlight gameplay\n67: - farming with multiple crops, including wheat and carrots\n68: - improved zombies\n69: - wave survival\n70: - NPC shop\n71: - progression\n72: - polished UI\n73: - multiple maps and biomes\n74: \n75: These items describe direction only. They are not permission to implement a\n76: system unless a specific approved task defines it.\n77: \n78: ## Quality and Scope Rules\n79: \n80: - Do not treat the rejected bedroom blockout as approved composition or art.\n81: - Its dimensions may be consulted only as rough reference.\n82: - Do not let legacy geometry or presentation define the rebuilt bunker.\n83: - Do not invent missing gameplay specifications.\n84: - Separate layout approval, art direction, gameplay implementation, and polish\n85:   into explicitly approved phases.\n\n(End of file - total 85 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"# THE OUTSKIRTS — Game Vision\n\n## Identity\n\n**Game:** THE OUTSKIRTS\n\nTHE OUTSKIRTS is an atmospheric survival game. The target is a polished,\ncohesive experience rather than a basic Roblox blockout or a collection of\nunconnected systems.\n\n## Target Experience\n\nThe player should feel vulnerable, curious, and motivated to make an abandoned\nplace functional again. Environments, gameplay systems, lighting, sound, UI,\nand progression should ultimately support the same survival atmosphere.\n\nThe intended quality bar is:\n\n- atmospheric\n- detailed","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/Users/Ori/Documents/Projects/BunkerGame/docs/director/GAME-VISION.md","text":"# THE OUTSKIRTS — Game Vision\n\n## Identity\n\n**Game:** THE OUTSKIRTS\n\nTHE OUTSKIRTS is an atmospheric survival game. The target is a polished,\ncohesive experience rather than a basic Roblox blockout or a collection of\nunconnected systems.\n\n## Target Experience\n\nThe player should feel vulnerable, curious, and motivated to make an abandoned\nplace functional again. Environments, gameplay systems, lighting, sound, UI,\nand progression should ultimately support the same survival atmosphere.\n\nThe intended quality bar is:\n\n- atmospheric\n- detailed\n- intentionally composed\n- abandoned but functional\n- survival-oriented\n- visually cohesive\n- significantly more polished than the current bunker\n\n## Starting Experience\n\nThe player wakes near an old bed inside a creepy, abandoned underground bunker\nbedroom.\n\nThe bedroom is the first readable space in a larger bunker. It must establish:\n\n- where the player has awakened\n- that the bunker is old, neglected, and still partly functional\n- a clear visual route toward the rest of the bunker\n- the survival tone of the wider game\n\nThe bedroom must connect into a larger bunker. It is not an isolated box and\nmust not be treated as a standalone final environment.\n\n## Bunker Vision\n\nThe bunker should be a sequence of purposeful, connected spaces rather than one\nrectangular room. The layout should eventually support:\n\n- bedroom/start area\n- central bunker/common area\n- weapon/workbench area\n- upgrade area\n- storage\n- power/electrical infrastructure\n- NPC/shop area\n- access toward farming and the outside\n- bunker entrance/defense point\n\nThese are spatial and long-term functional requirements. Missing gameplay\nbehavior must not be invented during environment planning.\n\n## Broader Gameplay Vision\n\nLong-term concepts include:\n\n- realistic-feeling rifle and combat gameplay\n- pickaxe/tool gameplay\n- torch/flashlight gameplay\n- farming with multiple crops, including wheat and carrots\n- improved zombies\n- wave survival\n- NPC shop\n- progression\n- polished UI\n- multiple maps and biomes\n\nThese items describe direction only. They are not permission to implement a\nsystem unless a specific approved task defines it.\n\n## Quality and Scope Rules\n\n- Do not treat the rejected bedroom blockout as approved composition or art.\n- Its dimensions may be consulted only as rough reference.\n- Do not let legacy geometry or presentation define the rebuilt bunker.\n- Do not invent missing gameplay specifications.\n- Separate layout approval, art direction, gameplay implementation, and polish\n  into explicitly approved phases.","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":85,"totalLines":85,"truncated":false}},"title":"BunkerGame/docs/director/GAME-VISION.md","time":{"start":1788122190129,"end":1788122190149}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_01a054634f1670b39f4351675b413ba7"}},"id":"prt_0546350ee001TdLHXm9yBnepiT","sessionID":"ses_fab9cc058ffexEheteSaWDsSOK","messageID":"msg_054634b2b001Qylg0Gr7c9FJ1v"}}
